This is a Beamer template set up to look pretty decent and have a
University of Notre Dame theme.  For math typesetting, it is definitely better than using existing Powerpoint templates.

The easiest way to install this theme is to just dump the *.sty files into the same directory as your tex source, along with the logos/ directory.

A minimal Beamer presentation using this template looks something like the following:

\documentclass{beamer}


\usetheme{NotreDame}
\begin{document}
%% Slides
\end{document}


The theme currently has 9 options:
	% nav - Enables a bottom right navigation bar
	% nologo - Removes the small logo from every slide's title bar
	% sections - Shows the current section name in a colored bar under the slide title
	% noslidenumbers - Removes counting of slides in bottom right
	% fullFooter - Enables a more descriptive footer (can't use noslidenumbers simultaneously)
	% cornerlogo - Draws a small academic mark in the bottom-left corner of every content frame
	% mark=primary|secondary - Which academic-mark lockup to use for the title page and corner logo
	%   primary   (default) - wide lockup, shield beside "University of Notre Dame"
	%   secondary           - compact vertical lockup, shield above "Notre Dame"
	% logo=fullcolor|black|blue|gold|gold-metallic|white - Which color variant of the mark/monogram to use (default: blue)
	% textcolor=blue|black - Body text color (default: blue, or black automatically if logo=black and textcolor isn't given)

Options are specified as:
  \usetheme[nav,mark=secondary,logo=gold]{NotreDame}

There is no dark/black-background color scheme -- this theme is always the white background. (An earlier [white] option, which switched between a black-background and white-background color theme, was removed in the Dowling Lab's September 2026 fork along with the dark theme itself.)

Two extra commands for a corner logo and a companion note box, in the white space beside it -- for a takeaway line, a reference list, anything short:

  \ndcornerlogo
    Draws the corner logo directly (called automatically as the frame
    background when [cornerlogo] is set; call it yourself, e.g. via
    \setbeamertemplate{background}{\ndcornerlogo}, for more control).

  \ndlogonote[align]{text}
    A note box horizontally centered between the corner logo's right
    edge and the slide's right edge, vertically centered on the logo's
    own vertical middle. [align] defaults to center (a short takeaway
    line); pass [left] for a left-aligned reference list. Measures the
    logo's actual rendered size, so it stays aligned with whichever
    [mark] is chosen.

  \ndcornerlogomargin, \ndcornerlogoheight
    Override with \renewcommand{...}{...} before \begin{document} to
    change the corner logo's distance from the page edge (default
    0.15mm) or its height (default 1.3cm).

Both use TikZ's "remember picture, overlay" to reference the page edges, which is standard TikZ behavior needing a second compilation pass to position correctly (the first pass doesn't yet know the page's absolute layout) -- a plain single `pdflatex` run will show them misplaced; `latexmk` (or any build that reruns until stable) handles this automatically.

Other suggested packages:
* tikz (pgf, for diagrams) -- already loaded by this theme, for the corner logo/note box
* listings (for source code listings)
* fontspec (if using xetex)

See included "main.tex" for suggested usage scenarios



Author: Daniel Howard (dhoward3@nd.edu)
Modified Release: February 2017

Adapted from author below:
Author: Tristan Ravitch (travitch@cs.wisc.edu)
Initial Release: June 2009
Public Domain

Forked and modernized by the Dowling Lab, September 2026: real official
Notre Dame marks (no college sub-branding, no outdated bundled logos),
a configurable mark/logo-color/text-color option system, a working
[sections] option, the dark color theme removed, and the corner-logo/
note-box commands. See beamerthemeNotreDame.sty's own header comment
for the full list of changes.


Extra
-----

Here is a very handy snippet of TeX to stick at
the beginning of your presentation (after \begin{document}):

\newcommand*{\alphabet}{ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz}
\newlength{\highlightheight}
\newlength{\highlightdepth}
\newlength{\highlightmargin}
\setlength{\highlightmargin}{2pt}
\settoheight{\highlightheight}{\alphabet}
\settodepth{\highlightdepth}{\alphabet}
\addtolength{\highlightheight}{\highlightmargin}
\addtolength{\highlightdepth}{\highlightmargin}
\addtolength{\highlightheight}{\highlightdepth}
\newcommand*{\Highlight}{\rlap{\textcolor{HighlightBackground}{\rule[-\highlightdepth]{\linewidth}{\highlightheight}}}}


HighlightBackground is defined by the NotreDame theme.
This snippet allows you to include source code listings in the
following way:

  \lstinputlisting[language=C,moredelim={**[il][\Highlight]{@}}]{file.c}

Note the moredelim option; with this option and the preceeding
declarations, prefixing a line in file.c will highlight the line.
